from lesson_data import P,S,E,Q,finish
LESSON=finish(dict(number=8,prereqs=[5,7],lead=P("Choose between divide and conquer, greedy choices, backtracking and dynamic programming. Justify optimality instead of trusting plausible choices.","在分治、贪心、回溯与动态规划间选择，论证最优性而非相信直觉。"),before=P("Know recursion and asymptotic bounds. The labs solve small scheduling and optimisation problems.","了解递归与渐近界。实验解决小型调度与优化问题。"),outcomes=[P("Recognise divide-and-conquer recurrences.","识别分治递推。"),P("Construct a greedy exchange argument.","构造贪心交换论证。"),P("Explore and prune search trees.","探索并剪枝搜索树。"),P("Define DP state and transitions.","定义动态规划状态与转移。"),P("Reconstruct and check solutions.","恢复并检查解。")],sections=[
S("Divide and conquer","分治","<p>Divide a problem into smaller instances, solve them, then combine. Merge sort satisfies T(n)=2T(n/2)+Θ(n) for balanced splits: each level does linear merge work and there are logarithmically many levels. Binary search solves only one half, so its recurrence is T(n)=T(n/2)+Θ(1). The number of subproblems and combine cost matter; saying 'uses recursion' alone does not identify a growth rate.</p>","<p>把问题分为小实例，求解后合并。归并排序平衡划分满足 T(n)=2T(n/2)+Θ(n)，每层线性、层数对数。二分仅解一半，为 T(n)=T(n/2)+Θ(1)。子问题数量与合并成本都重要，仅称递归不能确定增长。</p>","Why are merge sort and binary search different costs?","归并与二分为何成本不同？","Merge sort solves both halves and merges; binary search keeps only one half.","归并解两半并合并，二分只保留一半。"),
S("Greedy choices and exchange arguments","贪心选择与交换论证","<p>A greedy algorithm commits to a locally attractive choice. For maximum-count nonoverlapping intervals, choose earliest finish, then repeat on compatible intervals. An optimal schedule's first interval can be replaced by the earliest-finishing one without delaying any remaining start; this exchange leaves the count unchanged and reduces to the same residual problem. Earliest start lacks that argument: one long early interval can block many short ones. Maximising total interval value is a different problem and generally needs more than this rule.</p>","<p>贪心立即选择局部有利项。最多不重叠区间可选最早结束，再处理兼容区间。最优方案首区间可换成最早结束者，不推迟其他开始，数量不变，剩余仍同类问题。最早开始缺少此论证，早长区间可阻挡许多短区间。最大总价值是不同问题，通常不能用此规则。</p>","Does earliest finish solve weighted interval scheduling?","最早结束能解带价值区间调度吗？","Not generally; maximising value differs from maximising count.","一般不能，最大价值不同于最大数量。"),
S("Backtracking and exhaustive search","回溯与穷举","<p>Backtracking extends a partial solution, rejects impossible branches and undoes a choice before trying alternatives. For subsets of n items, there are 2^n choices before pruning. A constraint can reduce actual exploration without changing the worst-case exponential bound. Exhaustive search is useful as a small-instance oracle: compare a fast algorithm's answer with all feasible possibilities. Pruning must be justified; rejecting a merely unattractive partial choice can lose the optimum.</p>","<p>回溯扩展部分解，拒绝不可能分支，并撤销选择再试替代。n 项子集共 2^n 种，剪枝可能减少实际探索但最坏仍指数。小实例穷举可作为快速算法对照。剪枝需论证，不能因局部不够好就排除最优可能。</p>","Why keep exhaustive verification inputs small?","为何穷举验证输入需小？","The number of subsets grows exponentially.","子集数量指数增长。"),
S("Dynamic programming states","动态规划状态","<p>Dynamic programming reuses overlapping subproblem answers. For minimum coin count, define best[v] as the minimum count for amount v. Base best[0]=0; impossible states are infinity. Transition best[v]=min(best[v−c]+1) over positive coins c≤v. Compute increasing v so dependencies are ready. With k coin types and target A, time is O(kA), storage O(A). This is pseudo-polynomial in numeric A, not polynomial in the bit length of A. Greedy largest-coin-first fails for [1,3,4] at six: 4+1+1 loses to 3+3.</p>","<p>动态规划复用重叠子问题。best[v] 表示金额 v 最少硬币数，基础零，不可达为无穷。对正硬币 c≤v，取 best[v−c]+1 最小值。按 v 递增让依赖就绪。k 种硬币、目标 A 的时间 O(kA)、空间 O(A)，对数值 A 伪多项式，并非对 A 位长多项式。六元用 [1,3,4] 时贪心给 4+1+1，输给 3+3。</p>","Why must coin values be positive?","为何硬币值必须为正？","Transitions must move to smaller states; zero or negative values break that dependency order.","转移需到更小状态，零或负值破坏依赖顺序。"),
S("Reconstruction and independent checks","恢复与独立检查","<p>An optimum value alone may not tell the user what to do. Store the chosen predecessor at each improved state, then walk backwards to reconstruct decisions. Check feasibility independently: coin totals must equal the amount; intervals must not overlap. For a small case, compare optimality with exhaustive enumeration. This distinguishes implementation defects from a wrong recurrence. Specify unreachable and empty outcomes explicitly: amount zero has an empty valid solution, while an impossible positive amount has no solution.</p>","<p>只有最优值不一定告诉用户如何操作。每次改善状态保存选择的前驱，再逆向恢复。独立检查可行性：硬币总值等于目标，区间不重叠。小案例与穷举对照最优性，可区分实现错误与递推错误。零金额的空解有效，不可达正金额则无解。</p>","Are [] and None interchangeable DP results?","[] 与 None 可互换吗？","No. [] is a valid zero-amount solution; None means impossible.","不能，[] 是零金额有效解，None 表示无解。")],
labs=[dict(file="m08_greedy.py",title=P("Schedule intervals","区间调度"),intro=P("Maximise the count of compatible half-open intervals. Adjacent endpoints may touch. Exhaustive search checks this small instance.","最大化兼容半开区间数量，端点可相接，穷举检查小实例。"),tasks=P("<ol><li>Choose earliest start instead and construct a failure.</li><li>Add a zero-duration job and explain rejection.</li><li>Attach values to jobs and explain why the oracle must change.</li></ol>","<ol><li>改用最早开始，构造失败。</li><li>加零时长任务，解释拒绝。</li><li>为任务加价值，说明对照应如何改变。</li></ol>"),solution=P("<p>[0,10] blocks [1,2],[2,3],[3,4] under earliest start. The lab requires start&lt;finish, so zero duration is invalid. With values, maximise summed values instead of subset length and use a weighted algorithm.</p>","<p>最早开始的 [0,10] 阻挡三个短区间。实验要求开始小于结束，零时长无效。带价值需比较总价值而非数量，并采用带权算法。</p>")),dict(file="m08_dynamic.py",title=P("Minimum coins","最少硬币"),intro=P("Inspect every state for amount six and reconstruct the selected coins. Infinity marks unreachable states.","检查六元的各状态并恢复硬币，无穷标记不可达。"),tasks=P("<ol><li>Try [2,5] at amounts 1 and 7.</li><li>Compare greedy with DP for [1,3,4].</li><li>Add a count-only version and compare memory responsibilities.</li></ol>","<ol><li>测试 [2,5] 的一与七。</li><li>比较贪心与动态规划。</li><li>加入只返回数量的版本，比较存储职责。</li></ol>"),solution=P("<p>One is unreachable; seven uses 2 and 5. Six under [1,3,4] needs two coins, not the greedy three. A count-only version still stores best states but can omit reconstruction predecessors.</p>","<p>一不可达，七用二加五。[1,3,4] 的六需两枚，而非贪心三枚。仅计数仍需 best 状态，但可省恢复前驱。</p>"))],
exercises=[E(1,"Strategy","策略","Which strategy solves both halves then combines?","解两半再合并是什么策略？","<p>Divide and conquer.</p>","<p>分治。</p>"),E(1,"Coin counterexample","硬币反例","Compare greedy and optimum for coins 1,3,4 and amount 6.","比较六元的贪心与最优。","<p>Greedy: 4+1+1, three. Optimum: 3+3, two.</p>","<p>贪心三枚，最优两枚。</p>"),E(2,"State table","状态表","Give best[0…4] for coins 1,3,4.","给 [1,3,4] 的 best[0…4]。","<p>[0,1,2,1,1]. Each value uses ready smaller states.</p>","<p>[0,1,2,1,1]，依赖更小已就绪状态。</p>"),E(2,"Compatibility","兼容性","Can [1,3) and [3,5) both be selected?","[1,3) 与 [3,5) 可同时选吗？","<p>Yes; half-open intervals do not overlap at the shared endpoint.</p>","<p>可以，半开区间在共享端点不重叠。</p>"),E(2,"Subset growth","子集增长","How many subsets for 20 jobs?","二十任务多少子集？","<p>2^20=1,048,576, illustrating why exhaustive verification needs small n.</p>","<p>1,048,576，说明穷举需小规模。</p>"),E(3,"Exchange argument","交换论证","Explain why earliest finish can replace an optimal first interval.","说明最早结束如何替换最优首区间。","<p>It finishes no later, so every later interval still starts after its end. The count is preserved, and the residual scheduling problem has the same form.</p>","<p>结束不更晚，后续区间仍兼容，数量不变，剩余仍同类调度问题。</p>"),E(3,"DP proof","动态规划证明","Why does the coin recurrence consider every optimal solution?","硬币递推为何覆盖每个最优解？","<p>Any nonzero solution has a last coin c. Removing it leaves amount v−c; an optimal solution must use an optimal residual or replacing that residual would improve the whole. Minimise across all c.</p>","<p>非零解有最后硬币 c，移除剩 v−c。剩余若非最优，可替换改善整体，所以对所有 c 取最小。</p>"),E(2,"Numeric versus encoded size","数值与编码规模","Why is O(A) not polynomial in log₂ A?","为何 O(A) 不对 log₂ A 多项式？","<p>Writing A needs about log₂ A bits; A grows exponentially in that bit count. State whether size means value or encoded length.</p>","<p>A 需约 log₂ A 位，A 对位数指数增长，需说明规模指值还是编码长度。</p>")],
quiz=[Q("A greedy choice needs?","贪心选择需要什么？","An optimality argument","最优性论证","Only speed","仅速度","Recursion always","总是递归","Local attractiveness alone is insufficient.","局部吸引力不足。"),Q("Interval maximum-count rule?","最多区间选择规则？","Earliest finish","最早结束","Earliest start always","总最早开始","Longest duration","最长时长","An exchange preserves future feasibility.","交换保留后续可行性。"),Q("DP reuses?","动态规划复用什么？","Overlapping subproblems","重叠子问题","Random guesses","随机猜测","Only input bytes","仅输入字节","Memoisation or tables avoid repeated work.","记忆或表格避免重复工作。"),Q("best[0] for coin count?","硬币计数 best[0] 是多少？","0","0","Infinity","无穷","1","1","No coins make zero.","零无需硬币。"),Q("Backtracking worst-case subsets?","回溯最坏子集数？","2^n","2^n","n","n","log n","log n","Each item can be included or excluded.","每项可选或不选。"),Q("Reconstruction stores?","恢复保存什么？","Chosen predecessors","选择的前驱","Only a clock time","仅耗时","No choices","不保存选择","The value alone may not identify decisions.","仅数值未必确定决策。")],pitfalls=[P("Greedy correctness is specific to the objective and assumptions.","贪心正确性针对具体目标与假设。"),P("A DP table needs a state meaning and a valid dependency order.","动态规划表需状态含义与有效依赖顺序。")],reading=[(P("MIT algorithm materials","MIT 算法资料"),"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/6-006-introduction-to-algorithms-spring-2020/",P("Read dynamic programming; identify state, base and transition in an example.","阅读动态规划，在例子中指出状态、基础与转移。"))],terms=[(P("Optimal substructure","最优子结构"),P("An optimum can be assembled from appropriately optimal subproblems.","最优解可由合适的最优子问题组合。")),(P("Backtracking","回溯"),P("Explore choices, reject infeasible branches and undo choices.","探索选择，拒绝不可行分支并撤销。")),(P("Exchange argument","交换论证"),P("Replace an optimal choice without worsening the objective.","替换最优选择而不恶化目标。"))],review=P("<p>For a new optimisation task, define its objective, feasible solutions and state before choosing a strategy. Module 09 investigates the machine that executes these procedures.</p>","<p>对新优化任务先定义目标、可行解与状态，再选策略。模块 09 将研究执行这些过程的机器。</p>")))
